00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.200
I want to begin with a simple truth.

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:03.880
Often in the workplace today,

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:05.520
we're doing a lot of communicating

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:07.040
and not a lot of connecting.

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:10.360
What are you saying when you're not speaking?

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:12.920
It's those moments in between

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:16.400
where so much of that dialogue is happening.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.520
Because now leadership is more than the word

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:19.880
that just come out of our mouth.

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:22.080
It is about that connection.

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:24.000
And I wanna challenge you today to think about

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:26.280
how do you create that environment

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:29.480
where other people can show up smarter,

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:31.200
can show up more powerful,

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.280
can show up more productive.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:37.000
That's what we're going to begin to dig into today.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:40.200
My name is Stephen de Wit and I am a sexologist

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:42.880
and an expert in how humans connect.

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:46.040
We are facing an epidemic of disengagement

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:47.920
that drains performance

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:50.880
and that is driving your best people out the door.

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:54.600
I have sat down and worked with people

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:57.440
at the cutting edge of human behavior

00:00:57.440 --> 00:00:58.720
when they're struggling with things

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:00.480
that maybe you haven't even thought about

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:02.200
in your professional life.

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:04.560
Because the future is getting faster,

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:06.480
but where you can differentiate yourself

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:10.460
is leading human.

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:12.860
How you listen to someone

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:15.580
directly impacts how they show up.

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:17.100
We put that pressure on ourselves

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:20.420
that we have to be these expert communicators

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:22.380
where I really want you to lean in

00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:27.460
to be an expert connector.

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:29.940
The lead human model is built on one truth,

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:32.780
that performance follows connection.

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:35.860
When leaders develop their relational intelligence,

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:38.700
they learn how to read what's unspoken,

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:40.620
to be able to fix what's broken

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:43.660
and to be able to rebuild trust when that's been lost.

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:48.500
For when leaders choose to connect before they correct,

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:50.380
everything changes.

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:53.100
Trust deepens, engagement rises

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:55.420
and people feel safe to bring their bet.

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:58.100
Through the power of awareness and choice,

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:00.620
we can take that friction of leadership,

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:03.260
that silence, that tension,

00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:06.180
that unsaid defensiveness,

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:08.460
we can make that into fuel for connection,

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:11.140
where fear becomes curiosity,

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:13.860
where defensiveness becomes dialogue,

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:17.340
where pressure becomes presence.

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:21.500
Because when we choose connection over control,

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:22.940
not only do we lead better,

00:02:23.020 --> 00:02:25.700
but we build cultures people never want to lead.

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:28.620
Thank you for being in the room today with me

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:29.980
and doing the work.

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:31.140
I wish you all the best.
